# Pre login policy

- Finish and persist the login policy before resuming interrupted annaz/anna390 diagnostics.
- Only explicit pre password-authentication-stage failures may enter the existing OTP flow once.
- Missing business password, EMAIL_CODE requirements and rejected password authentication qualify.
- Joined-list, company, tenant, user, device, permission and post-authentication failures never qualify.
- Preserve all existing identity and authorization checks; never catch the entire pwd_login as fallback.
- For pre annaz, pin the reader mailbox to a16621325482@gmail.com regardless of global mailbox overrides.
- Keep annaz's real login_account as the business OTP recipient.
- Resolve that shared mailbox's own protected Password2/mailbox_password through the existing resolver.
- Never use annaz's other mailbox password for the shared mailbox or duplicate credential configuration.
- Preserve other routes, including Outlook proxy and anna390's own UserEmail plus Password2.
- Gmail uses Password2 only, never the SaaS Password as an app-password fallback.
- Remove Unicode whitespace from Gmail app passwords in memory only; require 16 ASCII letters.
- Missing or malformed app passwords fail immediately with sanitized configuration errors before sending.
- Do not modify workbook values or internal whitespace of ordinary non-Gmail passwords.
- Match the current send timestamp, trusted sender and actual recipient; reject stale or wrong-account OTP.
- Keep polling and resends bounded; log stages, counts and fixed error categories only.
- Never log OTP, passwords, tokens, full responses or request headers.
- Test remains fixed 123456 without password login; reuse valid sessions and refresh only on expiry.
- Do not change production, attendance idempotency prohibitions, permissions or unrelated scoring/work.
- Offline regressions mock network, mailbox and account getters; never run live test discovery.
- After policy verification resume authorized annaz/anna390 diagnosis, then pre cases, safe data repair,
  agreed primary/reviewer reports and Git publication; do not request repeated general authorization.
- Credentials stay in protected local configuration and never enter work-API context or Git.
